WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.190
Speaker 1: The Joe Biden White House is now
facing what is absolutely the biggest foreign

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:13.760
policy crisis of the still relatively new
presidency and administration of the Biden

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:20.750
White House, there has been an absolutely
terrible terrorist attack in Kabul, Afghanistan.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:28.470
This is part of the broader context of Joe
Biden deciding to make good, essentially on

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.490
the plan that Donald Trump claimed to have.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.659
Now, of course, Donald Trump ultimately did
not leave Afghanistan, essentially ran out

00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:42.420
of time, but as far as we knew, planned to
leave, just like Joe Biden ultimately decided

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.500
to do.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:50.019
And this is one of those areas where if you
are looking for the sort of simplistic black

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:56.190
or white Manichean analysis of what is going
on in Afghanistan, there's plenty of places

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.190
to get that.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.299
There's no question about it.

00:00:58.299 --> 00:01:05.440
And we've seen many of those simplistic analysis
analyzes come from the usual suspects, the

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.630
paid political consultants on both right and
left for different reasons.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:17.439
We've seen them come from the military industrial
complex, friendly, generally pro-war corporate

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:18.439
media.

00:01:18.439 --> 00:01:25.340
And by pro-war, I don't mean they want war
persay, but they want conflict and salaciousness.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:29.530
And they know that military conflicts generate
ratings.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.000
And unfortunately, all of those analyzes fall
short.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.829
And there's good and there's bad and there's
right and there's wrong.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:41.939
And it actually requires a little bit more
thinking in order to get something approximating

00:01:41.939 --> 00:01:46.359
a view that considers the totality of what
is going on.

00:01:46.359 --> 00:01:48.079
So we'll work backwards.

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:54.579
Thursday, two explosions happened in an area
right by the Kabul airport.

00:01:54.579 --> 00:02:01.060
This is an airport that has become a central
location in what is now taking place in Afghanistan,

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.950
which is many people trying to leave.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.250
There are Americans trying to leave.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:14.110
There are locals trying to leave and seek
asylum or refugee status in the United States

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.110
and elsewhere.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:21.130
As you are seeing the Taliban increasingly
prevent people from leaving to some degree.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:28.030
And also now we have introduced ISIS, ISIS
claiming responsibility for the two explosions.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.480
These were suicide bombings as of this morning.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:36.030
The latest numbers were one hundred and eighty
two people killed, including one hundred and

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:41.130
sixty nine Afghan civilians and 13 members
of the United States military.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:46.290
These are the first military casualties in
Afghanistan since February of twenty twenty.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:55.210
Joe Biden was meeting the remains of the 13
deceased American military members when they

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.950
arrived in the United States over the weekend.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:04.200
So let's go through each item here, because,
you know, it's actually kind of a bummer.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:09.490
I know that we're going to get really simple
black or white analysis from most in the media.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:14.060
The right is saying this is all terrible because
Biden's incompetent and Trump would have done

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.060
it great.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.060
Well, no, he would have won.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.370
No, no, he would not have.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:21.290
Some on the left are saying this was carried
out the wrong way.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:26.530
Biden was wrong to leave or just this is perfect
and everything has been gone swimmingly.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.540
All of these takes fall short.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.820
Joe Biden was 100 percent correct to leave.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.320
Afghanistan doesn't change anything about
that.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.900
Joe Biden was completely right to leave Afghanistan.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:45.090
This does not mean as a result of this terrorist
attack that we go back in my preference.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.090
Right.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.450
Of course we might.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.860
I don't believe it means we go back in, but
it does mean that Joe Biden has a crisis to

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:52.990
deal with here.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:59.390
Now, for those saying this crisis is what's
tanking, Joe Biden's approval and this crisis

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:02.820
is going to prevent Democrats from winning
in twenty to twenty two.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.690
I disagree and I disagree on both.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:08.180
And we're going to go into that more tomorrow,
the political implications of this part of

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.610
it as voters have a very short term memory.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:15.570
Part of it is foreign policy actually matters
surprisingly little when it comes to how people

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.670
vote in elections in the United States.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:19.190
We'll get back to that.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:25.580
But the fact that after just a few days of
the United States pulling back, you have the

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.500
Taliban taking over and then you have ISIS
versus the Taliban.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:36.500
This actually reinforces how completely untenable
our involvement was in Afghanistan.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.390
We have to stay forever in order to prevent
this.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:46.250
That's proof that we shouldn't be involved,
since the only way to keep things even relatively

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:50.100
calm, apparently, is to stay involved indefinitely.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.410
It's not viable.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:56.090
It's not viable unless you believe in the
United States as the never ending policeman

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.020
of the world, which I don't.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.020
That's not.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:02.830
My foreign policy view, I thought it wasn't
the view of a lot of trumpets when it was

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.630
Trump saying we're going to get out of there
now, all of a sudden those same people have

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.630
changed their mind.

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:09.780
I have not changed my mind on this.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.250
Trump should have left.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.250
Biden did leave.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.870
Obama should have left, but he didn't.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.320
OK, now, of course, the right is going after
Joe Biden.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:18.900
Well, yeah, Joe Biden is a Democrat.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.430
They're going to go after Joe Biden.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:24.530
Yes, this is a crisis, but it would have been
the same crisis under Donald Trump.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:29.850
We're seeing all the normal experts on foreign
policy come forward and say, oh, we should

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.020
have stayed.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:35.430
This is a humiliation for Biden, should have
gotten out differently.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:40.570
I have a completely different perspective
without denying that this has not gone well

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.480
because it hasn't gone well.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:48.850
We rarely see presidents act this decisively
in getting us out of a commitment around the

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:49.850
world.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:54.270
When presidents act decisively, it's usually
to start an incursion and it's considered

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:56.100
patriotic by the right.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:03.211
When George W. Bush said on my order, we have
started attacks in Iraq after 9/11 and all

00:06:03.211 --> 00:06:04.290
of this.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.290
Wow.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:06.290
Decisive and powerful.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:07.300
Well, hold on a second.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:11.690
Is it decisive and powerful to start an incursion
without actually thinking through the consequences

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:13.800
the way George W. Bush did?

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.169
This is the opposite, but it is decisive.

00:06:16.169 --> 00:06:22.181
Joe Biden has drawn a line and is getting
us out of what George W. Bush started, what

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:25.889
Barack Obama didn't end, what Donald Trump
didn't end.

00:06:25.889 --> 00:06:31.500
Biden is ending it in the first year of his
presidency.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.500
And that's good.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:36.020
And the situation has become very chaotic
and now Joe Biden has to figure out what to

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:44.020
do, but remember that the status quo before
we left was not some utopia for the Afghan

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:48.580
population, 200000 Afghans killed since we
went in.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:53.330
It's been chaotic for years in Afghanistan,
but nobody was paying attention.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:59.060
And now suddenly people are saying it only
just got chaotic because Joe Biden decided

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.060
to leave.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.060
That's wrong.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.900
It got more chaotic, without a doubt.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:07.620
And now we have pundits and so-called experts
saying the least interesting things.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:12.310
Just stay, stay for a month, stay for a year,
stay for another 20 years.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:18.040
How is that even considered remotely serious
unless your view of American foreign policy

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.530
is uber interventionist?

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:22.270
That's not my foreign policy.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:25.810
Joe Biden did a good thing by leaving left,
right.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.670
And corporate media in their own ways are
slamming him.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:31.530
But the decision was the right one.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.860
Now you have to figure out what to do with
the chaos.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:34.860
All the same.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:38.900
People who ignored this for decades are now
jumping in like they've been paying attention

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.510
and saying we should be staying or we should
have left this way or we should have let gimme

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:43.800
a break, guys.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:52.160
This is the same media that mostly rode willingly
into George W. Bush's Iraq war who are now

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.990
saying, oh, let's stay in Afghanistan, give
me a break.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:56.740
There are real problems.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:03.100
I don't understate for a second the dire situation
that is happening in Afghanistan.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:08.820
Life lost tragedy, but we've had that for
20 years and barely a peep from a lot of these

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.820
same people.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:15.479
Now, it's a cynical, uninformed attempt to
just go after Joe Biden.

00:08:15.479 --> 00:08:19.930
Joe Biden deserves criticism in all of this,
but leaving was the right decision.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:25.740
Trump should have left, Obama should have
left, resist the urge to demand that something

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:29.480
be either perfect or terrible.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:36.620
OK, reality is more complicated and it's too
complicated for the really predictable, boring,

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:42.099
hot takes that we are seeing, including from
all sorts of corporate media with various

00:08:42.099 --> 00:08:43.659
different political stripes.

00:08:43.659 --> 00:08:45.399
We're going to keep talking about it this
week.

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:46.399
By the way, one last thing.

00:08:46.399 --> 00:08:50.660
I got a few emails from people saying, David,
why haven't you talked about Afghanistan the

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.290
first week of this crisis?

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.290
I was gone.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:54.449
I just I was just wasn't here.

00:08:54.449 --> 00:08:56.509
My guest hosts talked about it.

00:08:56.509 --> 00:09:00.050
Since getting back, I've done nine segments
on Afghanistan.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:01.290
This today is number 10.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.610
Give me a break, guys.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:10:09.829
Find something else to complain about.

